{"id": "EUVD-2026-108791", "enisaUuid": "f10c8267-a2f8-34a3-94e4-1b6709333794", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/userq: only accept doorbell BOs as queue doorbell\n\namdgpu_userq_get_doorbell_index() pins any BO passed as doorbell_handle\ninto the doorbell domain. For a regular BO, TTM moves it with\nttm_bo_move_null() and its contents are lost. Since an importer on the\nsame device gets the exporter's GEM object, a client can do this to a\nbuffer another client shared with it.\n\nReject BOs that were not created in the doorbell domain.\n\nv2: drop the error message, use a local abo variable (Christian)\n\n(cherry picked from commit f7497bbc19db4821c62b9d97b31c9086feb2d917)", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:20:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:20:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/112dbe2b10d6d088a6c599980dd960dcbfa55ff0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8640b3f961d743d6dc0458c2b53a3af434690cc1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f7c88dbf4d543f6703e53bdeed380e886733167"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98997"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05f36bf9-131f-3868-baaa-060be99b3c07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3756de27-65b2-3153-a64a-1697f77b4253", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f09c1e6077abd1bc2ddd2b97e1135215801ca7f9 <8640b3f961d743d6dc0458c2b53a3af434690cc1"}, {"id": "3d031ef0-a69c-3609-ae45-a6c80385f56a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f09c1e6077abd1bc2ddd2b97e1135215801ca7f9 <7f7c88dbf4d543f6703e53bdeed380e886733167"}, {"id": "afa3e4f5-4589-321a-bae0-ce97285b8b12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "be87a2e1-0521-3d14-9914-071868dd40c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_ver